course: dictionary
lesson: 2057
title: Consent: saying yes, and saying no
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Consent means giving permission, or agreeing to something happening. You will meet this word at school, at the doctor's and online. «Taking and sharing photos of people without asking can upset them, and consent means agreeing, so you should ask before you post.» The key idea is a clear yes that comes before something happens.
explain: At school, a trip needs a parent's consent form, which is a signed yes. Before an operation, «doctors explain it, its risks and benefits», and children are asked to agree too and may ask any question. You have the right to ask questions before you say yes.
explain: Consent works both ways. Your body is yours, so nobody should touch you without your consent. If someone asks you to do something that makes you feel unsafe or uncomfortable, you can say no and tell a grown-up you trust straight away. A no always counts.
explain: Look at the clues in context. «The British Empire ... ruled many people without their consent» tells you they were ruled without being asked or agreeing. Swap in your meaning: "ruled many people without their permission" still makes sense, so consent means permission.
fact: Consent means permission, or agreeing to let something happen.
fact: As a verb, «to consent» means to agree or give permission, and «consented» is its past tense.
fact: «With the consent of» is a formal phrase meaning with someone's permission.
fact: A consent form is a paper a parent signs to say yes to a school trip or a medical treatment.
fact: Without consent, no one should touch you or share your photo.
exercise: «Before an operation ... a parent signs a consent form.» What is a consent form? | A list of the day's homework | A form for ordering food at lunch | A ticket for the school bus | *A paper that is a signed yes, giving permission
exercise: Sam wants to post a photo of Priya online. What should Sam do first? | Send it only to a few friends | Post it quickly before she notices | Change the colours and then post it | *Ask Priya for her consent before posting
exercise: Which word means to agree or give permission, in the past tense? | consenting | consents | *consented | consent-ing-ed
test: In «ruled many people without their consent», what does consent mean? | Money and land | A loud argument | Being cheerful about something | *Permission or agreement
test: Your friend says «no» to a hug. What should you do? | Hug them quickly while they are not looking | Hug them anyway, because they will feel better | Ask three other friends to decide for them | *Respect the no and stop
exam: Which statement about consent is true? | *Consent is a clear yes, and a no is always a valid answer | Once someone says yes, they can never change their mind | Silence always means yes | Consent only matters for grown-ups
